From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 13:32:39 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Let the network cards wake the laptop

The OEM firmware lets the Gigabit Ethernet controller and the Wi-Fi and
WWAN cards wake the laptop from S3 and S4: _PRW on the Ethernet device
(PME, GPE 0x0d, as the USB controllers) and on their root ports (PCIe
PME, GPE 0x09). The DSDT had no device for the Ethernet controller at
all, so Wake-on-LAN could not be enabled, and no _PRW on the ports. Add
them; the OS enables each wake source on request only.

TEST=ThinkPad W541: the DSDT compiles with GLAN and the _PRW entries.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
index f7e6ecae..08af061a 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/dsdt.asl
@@ -42,6 +42,22 @@ DefinitionBlock(
 		Scope (RP02) { Device (PXSX) { Name (_ADR, 0) } }
 		Scope (RP03) { Device (PXSX) { Name (_ADR, 0) } }
 		Scope (RP05) { Device (PXSX) { Name (_ADR, 0) } }
+
+		/*
+		 * What can wake the laptop, as on the OEM firmware: the Gigabit
+		 * Ethernet controller (Wake-on-LAN, its PME on GPE 0x0d like the
+		 * USB controllers) and the Wi-Fi and WWAN cards (PCIe PME, GPE
+		 * 0x09), from S3 and S4. The OS enables each one on request
+		 * (ethtool -s ... wol g, /sys/.../power/wakeup).
+		 */
+		Device (GLAN)
+		{
+			Name (_ADR, 0x00190000)
+			Name (_S3D, 3)
+			Name (_PRW, Package () { 0x0d, 4 })
+		}
+		Scope (RP02) { Name (_PRW, Package () { 0x09, 4 }) }
+		Scope (RP03) { Name (_PRW, Package () { 0x09, 4 }) }
 	}
 
 #if CONFIG(LENOVO_HASWELL_DGPU_RUNTIME_PM)
